{{fbdoc item="title" value="Freetype2"}}----
A Free, High-Quality, and Portable Font Engine

Website: http://www.freetype.org
Platforms supported: Windows, Linux
Headers to include: freetype2/freetype.bi
Header version: 2.5.5
Examples: yes, in ""examples/graphics/FreeType/""

The Windows examples were checked with the genuine FreeType 2.14.3 SDK on Win32 and Win64. Their optional first command-line argument selects a font file; the fallback remains the platform-specific example font. A missing font returns a nonzero status.

A glyph bitmap belongs to its face and remains valid until another glyph is loaded or the face is released. Destroy the face before the library. The examples render eight-bit grayscale coverage; other pixel modes need their own interpretation or an explicit conversion.

The text renderer uses ##ULong## for each 32-bit destination pixel. ##UInteger## is pointer-sized and occupies eight bytes on Win64. ##ScreenInfo## supplies the actual destination pitch. The caller holds ##ScreenLock## while the renderer writes into the framebuffer.

##bitmap.bi## clips each glyph independently and honors padding and signed source pitch. A negative-pitch bitmap stores its bottom row at the buffer base, so its top row begins at a higher address. Coverage is blended with division by 255, which makes full coverage replace the destination pixel exactly. The example's text loop handles individual bytes; it is not a Unicode shaping engine.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/freetype2.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' Example of rendering a char using freetype

#include "freetype2/freetype.bi"

#ifdef __FB_LINUX__
Const TTF_FONT = "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/ttf-dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf"
#else
Const TTF_FONT = "Vera.ttf"
#endif

Sub releaseFreeType(ByRef library As FT_Library, ByRef face As FT_Face)

	If face <> 0 Then
		FT_Done_Face face
		face = 0
	End If

	If library <> 0 Then
		FT_Done_FreeType library
		library = 0
	End If

End Sub

Dim font_file As String = Command(1)
If font_file = "" Then font_file = TTF_FONT

Dim As FT_Library library = 0
Dim As FT_Face face = 0

If (FT_Init_FreeType(@library) <> 0) Then
	Print "FT_Init_FreeType() failed" : End 1
End If

''
'' Load a font and render an '@' character on to a bitmap
''

If (FT_New_Face(library, font_file, 0, @face) <> 0) Then
	releaseFreeType library, face
	Print "FT_New_Face() failed (font file '" & font_file & "' not found?)" : End 1
End If

If (FT_Set_Pixel_Sizes(face, 0, 200) <> 0) Then
	releaseFreeType library, face
	Print "FT_Set_Pixel_Sizes() failed" : End 1
End If

If (FT_Load_Char(face, Asc("@"), FT_LOAD_DEFAULT) <> 0) Then
	releaseFreeType library, face
	Print "FT_Load_Char() failed" : End 1
End If

If (FT_Render_Glyph(face->glyph, FT_RENDER_MODE_NORMAL) <> 0) Then
	releaseFreeType library, face
	Print "FT_Render_Glyph() failed" : End 1
End If

''
'' Draw the rendered bitmap
''

If ScreenRes(320, 200, 32) <> 0 Then
	releaseFreeType library, face
	Print "Could not set the requested graphics mode"
	End 1
End If

Dim As FT_Bitmap Ptr bitmap = @face->glyph->bitmap
If bitmap->pixel_mode <> FT_PIXEL_MODE_GRAY Or bitmap->num_grays <> 256 Or bitmap->buffer = NULL Then
    releaseFreeType library, face
    End 1
End If
Dim row_size As LongInt = Abs(CLngInt(bitmap->pitch))
If row_size < bitmap->width Or bitmap->width > 8192 Or bitmap->rows > 8192 Then
    releaseFreeType library, face
    End 1
End If
Dim source_top As UByte Ptr = bitmap->buffer
If bitmap->pitch < 0 Then source_top += row_size*(bitmap->rows-1)


For y As Integer = 0 To (bitmap->rows - 1)
	For x As Integer = 0 To (bitmap->Width - 1)
		Dim As Integer col = source_top[y * CLngInt(bitmap->pitch) + x]
		PSet(x, y), RGB(col, col, col)
	Next
Next

Sleep

releaseFreeType library, face

'' end of freetype2.bas
%%

